"title": "Sheet-metal enclosure",
"author": "3DCraft Jigs",
"licence": "CC-BY-4.0",
"description": "A two-part sheet-metal electronics case, sized from what goes in it: a board, a power supply or a stack of boards. A chassis (floor, front and back walls, return flanges with clinch nuts) and a cover (top and two sides), each laser cut and bent on a press brake from one sheet, in steel, aluminium or stainless at stock thicknesses. The bend radius, K-factor, die and minimum leg come from a shop's published bending table and the material's standard; bend order is proven at every form change. Export: file.export with sheetMetal for Chassis and Cover (or the menu's flat patterns of every part) writes DXF flat patterns with bend lines, no picking.",
